WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:06.879
Watchmen is one of the most popular and influential
comic books ever, written in the 80s by English

00:00:06.879 --> 00:00:08.620
wizard Alan Moore.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:13.660
Watchmen is a superhero story that questions
the idea of a hero – which is symbolised

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.170
by this bloody smiley face.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:21.280
The smiley is the ultimate simplistic cartoon,
representing the optimism of comic books where

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:27.060
good guys fight bad guys and no one ever really
dies . Watchmen splashes that smiley with

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:33.289
blood, cause it adds flawed human characters,
moral ambiguity, politics, philosophy, and

00:00:33.289 --> 00:00:36.079
darkness that was unusual in comics at the
time.

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:41.370
Of course now, everything’s a dark gritty
reimagining of superheros – but Watchmen

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:46.809
did it before it was cool, and still holds
up as a complex story about power, morality,

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:49.550
fantasy, and giant psychic squids.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:54.420
So what happens in the original Watchmen,
and what does it mean?

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.899
The story’s set in an alternate 80s America,
where superheroes exist.

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:03.239
None of them have superpowers – they’re
just vigilantes in costumes.

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:07.260
Except for Dr. Manhattan, who has like all
the powers, except pants.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:12.659
With Manhattan’s help, America won the Vietnam
War, and Richard Nixon is still president

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:14.579
– he’s on his fifth term.

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:18.680
A hero called the Comedian does dirty work
for the government, and it’s hinted that

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:23.990
he covered up the Watergate scandal, which
in the real world ended Nixon’s presidency.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:29.340
So superheroes change the course of history,
and they also affect culture.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:34.439
The hero Silk Spectre was a celebrity and
sex symbol in the 40s , and Ozymandias built

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:39.899
a corporate empire selling action figures
of himself . Because of all the real superheroes,

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:44.859
people lost interest in superhero comics,
so comics about pirates are popular instead.

00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:50.210
Thanks to Dr. Manhattan, technology’s more
advanced – 80s New York has electric cars

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.619
and airships, and people eat genetically-modified
four-legged chicken.

00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:59.420
In the 70s, heroes were outlawed, so most
of them retired – only Manhattan and the

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.619
Comedian are allowed to keep working for the
government.

00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:08.229
When the story starts, tension is rising in
the Cold War between America and Russia – everyone

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:15.070
fears nuclear annihilation, the doomsday clock
approaches midnight, and the Comedian is mysteriously

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.290
killed.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:21.110
The murder’s investigated by Rorschach,
a hero who refused to retire.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:25.750
On the surface, Rorschach is like Batman – he
lurks in the shadows, beats up criminals,

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:31.720
says edgy shit in a gravelly voice . But by
day, Batman is Bruce Wayne, a sexy genius

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:32.720
billionaire.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.740
While Rorschach is Walter Kovacs, a greasy
loner weirdo who walks the streets with a

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.050
sign saying “The end is nigh”.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:44.490
Cause realistically, the sort of person who
dresses up and fights people at night isn’t

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:50.980
a functional person – he’s “a nutcase”
. So Rorschach is an asocial violent psycho

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.130
with an extreme worldview.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:58.730
He thinks all of society is filthy and sinful
and doesn’t deserve mercy . Rorschach’s

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:03.850
black-and-white mask reflects his black-and-white
morality – everything’s either good or

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:10.270
evil, and evil must be punished . He says
he never compromises in his judgement , but

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:15.910
he’s often biased – he spares people punishment
for personal reasons, and like, when he hears

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:20.480
the Comedian tried to rape Silk Spectre, he
doesn’t care, cause he sees the Comedian

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:26.790
as a patriot , and Silk Spectre as a “whore”
. Rorschach is psychologically disturbed by

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:32.850
sex . As a kid, his mother was abusive, and
he saw her working as a prostitute – sexuality

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:38.240
reminds Rorschach of his hatred and disgust
for his mother , and he expresses this anger

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.810
by fighting criminals . Rorschach became a
vigilante when he heard about Kitty Genovese,

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:49.331
a real-world murder victim in the 60s . Rorschach
was still a kind of “rational” person

00:03:49.331 --> 00:03:53.960
back then , until he discovered the savage
murder of a child.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:59.310
Rorschach saw the darkest side of humanity,
and it broke him, convinced him that the world

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:05.560
is random and godless and has “No meaning”
– “save what we choose to impose”.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:10.480
The only way Rorschach could save himself
from despair and trauma was to impose his

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:15.120
brutal ideology, punishing evil no matter
the cost.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.880
Which often just causes more suffering . Like,
he routinely gets information by breaking

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:26.910
random peoples’ fingers until he hears something
useful . He terrorises a sick old man, and

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.840
breaks into peoples houses and eats all their
beans.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.480
Rorschach calls everyone else “parasites”,
but he’s the one who lives off other people

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:40.630
. Rorschach calls everyone filth – but he’s
the one who stinks . He says he never compromises,

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.160
but he often does.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:47.600
And his obsession with punishing evil just
leaves more bloody footprints behind him.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:52.541
So Watchmen goes deep into the psychology
of the masked avenger, and it doesn’t find

00:04:52.541 --> 00:04:59.730
a cool hero like Batman – Rorschach is a
gross, hypocritical sad broken man.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:05.660
But Rorschach does help uncover a conspiracy
that threatens millions of people…

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:10.180
Dr. Manhattan explores what it means to be
superhuman.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:15.540
He can effortlessly shape the world around
him on an atomic scale , he can teleport , walk

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:22.200
on the sun, sees past present and future as
one . He’s like a god , but he’s a really

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.510
shitty boyfriend.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:29.170
Cause being superhuman makes it hard to relate
with people , he doesn’t have human needs

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:34.120
or human fears, he’s cold and distant, and
really bad at sex.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:39.880
Manhattan can see the universe, from the dance
of atoms, to ancient Martian geology, so humans

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:45.830
are like ants to him – their lives so small
and short . The people around him age and

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.350
die, but he never changes.

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:52.620
When he starts relationships, he already sees
the future when they’ll break up . Through

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:57.900
the medium of comics, we get to see the time
as Manhattan does – with past present and

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:03.960
future all visible at once, a story with a
predetermined end.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:08.560
Manhattan says that free will is illusion
– that “We’re all puppets”, he’s

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:13.460
“just a puppet who can see the strings”
. So in a way, the most powerful being in

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:20.120
the universe is powerless – he can’t change
the future, cause to him, it’s already happened.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:24.180
Manhattan’s superhuman perspective makes
him not human.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:28.530
And without human feelings, he has no desire
to be a superhero and save the world.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:34.020
So, Manhattan is a deconstruction of characters
like Superman – suggesting that a superhuman

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.770
would actually not be a great protector of
humans.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:43.370
There’s something existentially terrifying
about a being so powerful – he makes regular

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:50.260
humans irrelevant, obsolete, like Neanderthals
replaced by sapiens . Manhattan gets falsely

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:55.600
accused of giving people cancer, and his girlfriend
Laurie leaves him for an owl man.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.870
So Manhattan fucks off to Mars and builds
a sandcastle.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:03.680
Eventually, Laurie convinces Manhattan that
human life does have value, because of its

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:06.699
sheer miraculous improbability.

00:07:06.699 --> 00:07:11.500
And that, by the way, is a real actual smiley
face on Mars.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:16.270
So Manhattan returns to Earth to try to prevent
apocalypse.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:18.420
Nite Owl is a retired hero.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:22.150
Back in the day, he dressed like an owl and
used gadgets to fight crime.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.290
But now, he finds that stuff embarrassing.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:29.700
He realised that punching criminals doesn’t
actually make the world better – and all

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:35.590
the costumes and gadgets were a “childish”
“fantasy” . So now Nite Owl is just Dan

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:36.590
Dreiberg.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:40.400
He’s in his forties, he gained weight, like
Batman with fupa, and he’s not happy.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:45.460
Rorschach warns him of a conspiracy, and the
threat of war, but Dan feels powerless to

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.150
face these dangers.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:52.930
He feels lonely and useless and “impotent”
. He wants to be with Laurie, but he’s awkward

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:57.370
and unconfident . When they try to have sex,
Dan can’t get it up – there’s something

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:03.550
missing from his life, until Dan and Laurie
rediscover the excitement of being heroes.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:07.040
They get back into costume, and spring Rorschach
from jail.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:11.960
The power and danger and fun of it sparks
magic in their relationship – and being

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:17.430
an owl really gets Dan’s dick hard . So
superheroes are silly and childish, but there’s

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.290
still meaning there.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:23.740
Dan writes an essay about ornithology, the
scientific study of birds.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:29.110
He says sometimes science loses the beauty
and poetry of nature, and there’s no point

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:32.880
in life if you’re all sensible and rational
all the time.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:38.899
We need wonder and romance and silliness because
it’s fun, and it brings people together.

00:08:38.899 --> 00:08:44.159
Dan and Laurie fall in love, and embrace their
heroic identities, and face the looming threat

00:08:44.159 --> 00:08:47.180
of nuclear war.

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:51.589
Laurie is the most normal person among the
superheroes, probably because she never really

00:08:51.589 --> 00:08:53.259
wanted to be a superhero.

00:08:53.259 --> 00:08:58.439
Her mother Sally was the original Silk Spectre,
and she pushed Laurie into being Silk Spectre

00:08:58.439 --> 00:09:03.839
II, making her train for her hero career,
like one of those beauty pageant moms.

00:09:03.839 --> 00:09:09.200
Laurie hates the Comedian, because he once
tried to rape her mother Sally.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:13.629
But Laurie discovers that that later on, Sally
loved the Comedian anyway, and they had a

00:09:13.629 --> 00:09:19.120
child together – turns out the Comedian,
the most despicable character in Watchmen,

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:26.110
is Laurie’s father . So Laurie smashes a
bottle of Nostalgia brand perfume, her childhood

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:31.640
snow globe smashes, Manhattan’s Martian
castle smashes, Laurie’s whole idea of who

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:38.040
she is collapses, becomes something messier
and darker . Cause she later plans to change

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:44.680
her costume to something similar to the Comedian’s,
as though she partly embraces his legacy – in

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:49.809
the upcoming Watchmen TV show, Laurie takes
the Comedian’s surname, Blake.

00:09:49.809 --> 00:09:55.649
So this revelation is a loss of innocence,
for Laurie and for superheroes, which is what

00:09:55.649 --> 00:09:58.589
Watchmen’s bloody smiley represents.

00:09:58.589 --> 00:10:03.350
Overall though, Laurie’s character isn’t
explored as deeply as the other characters.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:08.220
She and her mother are largely defined by
their sexuality and relationships with men.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:13.660
So depictions of women is one comics trope
that Watchmen does little to subvert.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:20.759
In the end, Laurie, Dan, Manhattan and Rorschach
discover a conspiracy masterminded by Ozymandias.

00:10:20.759 --> 00:10:27.109
Ozymandias is Adrian Veidt, another retired
hero, said to be the “smartest man on Earth”

00:10:27.109 --> 00:10:33.149
. Veidt is a super ambitious super rich super
arrogant dude who wants to be like Alexander

00:10:33.149 --> 00:10:39.309
the Great, and the Egyptian pharaohs . His
dream is to unite the world – under his

00:10:39.309 --> 00:10:45.449
design . Veidt realised that superheroes couldn’t
save the world from nuclear war . So instead,

00:10:45.449 --> 00:10:48.059
he hatched a crazy plan.

00:10:48.059 --> 00:10:52.579
He put a bunch of scientists and artists on
a secret island and genetically engineered

00:10:52.579 --> 00:10:55.259
a giant psychic squid monster.

00:10:55.259 --> 00:11:00.149
He kills the Comedian when the Comedian finds
out his plan, and he uses a cancer hoax to

00:11:00.149 --> 00:11:05.759
get rid of Manhattan , and frames Rorschach
to get him jailed, and he hires an assassin

00:11:05.759 --> 00:11:11.589
on himself to throw off suspicion, and finally
he teleports the squid into New York, killing

00:11:11.589 --> 00:11:17.000
three million people, to make it look like
aliens attacked, to scare the world into ending

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:23.949
the Cold War, uniting humanity, and bringing
peace on Earth . It’s a crazy supervillain

00:11:23.949 --> 00:11:26.529
plan, and it actually succeeds.

00:11:26.529 --> 00:11:31.829
America and Russia are so freaked out by the
supposed alien that they make a peace deal.

00:11:31.829 --> 00:11:38.279
And Rorschach and Manhattan and Dan and Laurie
fail to stop Ozymandias from killing millions

00:11:38.279 --> 00:11:40.490
of people – so much for superheroes.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:45.189
Ozymandias saves the world not by punching
anyone, and not with superhuman powers, but

00:11:45.189 --> 00:11:51.820
by science and determination and a psychopathic
willingness to kill three million people.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:59.289
He saves the world at a terrible cost – so
is he a hero, or a villain?

00:11:59.289 --> 00:12:04.300
Throughout Watchmen, there’s a comic book
within the comic book, a tale of the Black

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.300
Freighter.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:10.499
It’s a story about a sailor who tries to
save his town from an apocalyptic pirate ship,

00:12:10.499 --> 00:12:14.959
but he ends up killing innocent people, and
becoming just as evil as what he tried to

00:12:14.959 --> 00:12:20.679
prevent – “Noble intentions” led him
to “to atrocity” – just like Ozymandias’

00:12:20.679 --> 00:12:21.679
plan.

00:12:21.679 --> 00:12:26.170
At the end of Watchmen, Ozymandias has a dream
of the Black Freighter , and his last panel

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:29.939
shows him alone, separate from the world.

00:12:29.939 --> 00:12:34.569
Like the sailor, he is “marooned from the
rest of humanity” because of the evil he

00:12:34.569 --> 00:12:40.629
did . But Ozymandias says that “someone
had to take the weight of that awful, necessary

00:12:40.629 --> 00:12:45.550
crime” . This pose looks kinda like the
crucifixion of Christ.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:51.649
And we later see an ad for the Tarkovsky movie
The Sacrifice, in which a man sacrifices everything

00:12:51.649 --> 00:12:54.100
he loves to prevent war.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:59.930
Maybe you can see Ozymandias’ plan as a
heroic self-sacrifice – he did the terrible

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:04.110
necessary crime so no one else had to.

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:09.579
Or you can say he’s a delusional egomaniacal
mass-murdering psychopath, and a criticism

00:13:09.579 --> 00:13:13.559
of rich assholes having way too much power
in the world in the first place.

00:13:13.559 --> 00:13:19.420
Does Ozymandias really care about saving people,
or is her serving his pride and ambition.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:25.060
Philosophically, Ozymandias’ plan is utilitarian
– he kills three million people to save

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:29.410
the entire world, so the good outweighs the
evil.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:35.470
But Rorschach doesn’t believe in moral grey
area – he sees just black and white.

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:40.829
So he wants to reveal the truth of Ozymandias’
crimes, to punish him – even though revealing

00:13:40.829 --> 00:13:44.769
the truth of his alien hoax would destroy
the new world peace.

00:13:44.769 --> 00:13:50.420
Rorschach says he will “Never compromise”,
“Not even in the face of Armageddon” . So

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:53.860
Manhattan kills Rorschach to keep the secret.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:59.230
In his final moment, Rorschach takes off his
mask, and dies as Walter Kovacs, showing his

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:03.660
humanity and vulnerability in the end, cause
deep down, under the anger, Rorschach’s

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:11.110
just a broken lonely man who’s craved death
from the start .Rorschach’s inflexible morals

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:16.149
can’t survive in a morally complex world,
so it seems that his black-and-white morality

00:14:16.149 --> 00:14:17.339
fails.

00:14:17.339 --> 00:14:23.049
But – we see earlier, that Rorschach wrote
notes about Ozymandias’ conspiracy, and

00:14:23.049 --> 00:14:27.689
sent them to a journalist, who may or may
not reveal the truth to the world.

00:14:27.689 --> 00:14:34.499
The last line of Watchmen is “I leave it
entirely in your hands” . So when you close

00:14:34.499 --> 00:14:38.809
the comic book in your hands, you decide what
the ending means.

00:14:38.809 --> 00:14:44.959
Maybe Ozymandias’ hoax is revealed – maybe
Rorschach was right, and Ozy deserves punishment,

00:14:44.959 --> 00:14:47.399
even if it risks nuclear war.

00:14:47.399 --> 00:14:52.589
Or maybe you believe in Ozymandias’ brave
new world, even though it’s built on murder

00:14:52.589 --> 00:14:53.809
and lies.

00:14:53.809 --> 00:14:55.759
Or maybe you feel like Dr. Manhattan.

00:14:55.759 --> 00:15:00.459
He decides that humans are too annoying and
complicated, so he leaves the galaxy, to create

00:15:00.459 --> 00:15:06.319
life elsewhere – there’s no place for
a superhuman among humans, in the end.

00:15:06.319 --> 00:15:08.899
Or maybe you relate to Dan and Laurie.

00:15:08.899 --> 00:15:13.290
They don’t save the world , or die for a
cause.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:18.279
But they do get a happy ending – they fall
in love, take new identities, and start a

00:15:18.279 --> 00:15:22.069
life together, planning to continue being
superheroes.

00:15:22.069 --> 00:15:24.819
They know that being heroes doesn’t achieve
much.

00:15:24.819 --> 00:15:27.459
They know it’s childish and dangerous.

00:15:27.459 --> 00:15:30.699
But they embrace the fun and romance of it.

00:15:30.699 --> 00:15:36.389
Watchmen is a criticism of the fantasy of
the superhero, showing that reality is darker

00:15:36.389 --> 00:15:39.129
and more complicated than we like to admit.

00:15:39.129 --> 00:15:43.940
But despite that, Dan and Laurie’s story
reminds us that for all fantasy’s flaws,

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:49.990
it brings joy and meaning to peoples’ lives
. The smiley is bloodied, the snow globe broke,

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:52.859
the perfume smashed, millions died.

00:15:52.859 --> 00:15:54.079
We grew up.

00:15:54.079 --> 00:15:58.319
But we can still have nostalgia for simpler
times.

00:15:58.319 --> 00:16:01.230
In the end, Watchmen is a Rorschach test.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:05.810
Everyone has a different interpretation of
the story, depending on which characters and

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:11.920
ideas resonate with you – it’s entirely
in your hands.

